    "body": "## What?\r\n\r\nCrush now tells the terminal what it is doing, using the [Program Status Protocol (OSC 7501)](https://www.superlogical.com/rex/docs/build/program-status):\r\n\r\n\r\n\u2022 Working: the agent or a `!` shell command is running.\r\n\u2022 Blocked: Crush is waiting on you for a permission prompt, a question form, or AWS sign-in.\r\n\u2022 Done / Error: the last turn finished or failed. This stays until you submit a new prompt or switch back to the terminal window.\r\n\u2022 Idle: otherwise.\r\n\r\nBumps bubbletea (with matching ultraviolet and x/ansi) to a pinned commit\r\n\r\n## Why?\r\n\r\nUsers run Crush in a background tab and miss when it needs approval or has finished. Terminals that support OSC 7501 can show this in tab indicators and send notifications without guessing from the screen. Terminals that don't support it ignore the sequence.",
